THE INDIVIDUAL USE LICENCE

Version 1.0.0

Identifier: IUL-1.0.0

<<LICENCE URL>>

## Preamble

This licence is free for people. It is free for small outfits. It is not free
for large organisations, because large organisations can afford it and have
spent thirty years pretending otherwise.

It is not open source, and you must not call it open source. Open source asks
nothing of a company with a billion dollars and nothing of a person with a
laptop. These terms ask a great deal of the first and nothing at all of the
second.

It also says something older licences do not: what happens when software is
written by a machine, and what happens when it is fed to one.

Take it. Use it. Pay for it if you are large enough to be worth charging.

## Purpose

These terms let any individual person use, change and share this software for
free, and let small organisations do the same. They guarantee that fair,
reasonable and non-discriminatory terms for a paid licence will be available to
everyone else.

They exist so that a person can write software without becoming a company, a
support desk or a supplicant, and so that the organisations best able to pay for
software are the ones who do.

## Acceptance

In order to get any licence under these terms, you must agree to them as both
strict obligations and conditions of all your licences.

## Individual Use

If you are a natural person, you may use the software for any purpose, including
commercial purposes.

Use is Individual Use when the benefit of it goes to you as a natural person and
not to an organisation. Working alone, for yourself, on your own account, is
Individual Use whether or not you are paid for it, and whether or not you are
self-employed.

## Small Organisation

You may use the software for the benefit of an organisation if it meets all of
these criteria:

1. it had fewer than 8 total individuals working as employees and independent
   contractors at all times during its last tax year;

2. it earned less than $400,000 total revenue in its last tax year;

3. it received less than $400,000 total debt, equity and other investment in its
   last five tax years, counting investment in predecessor organisations that
   reorganised into, merged with, or spun out of it.

All dollar figures are United States dollars as of 2019. Adjust them for
inflation according to the United States Bureau of Labor Statistics' consumer
price index for all urban consumers, United States city average, for all items,
not seasonally adjusted, with 1982-1984=100 reference base.

## Paid Use

You may use the software for the benefit of an organisation that does not
qualify under Small Organisation:

1. for 128 days after it stops qualifying under Small Organisation; and

2. indefinitely, if the licensor or their legal successor does not offer fair,
   reasonable and non-discriminatory terms for a paid licence for the software
   within 32 days of a written request and negotiate in good faith to conclude a
   deal.

## How to Request a Paid Licence

Write to <<LICENCE CONTACT>>.

If this software includes an address for the licensor or an agent of the
licensor in a standard place, such as in documentation, software package
metadata, or an "about" page or screen, try to request fair terms at that
address. If this software includes both online and offline addresses, try online
before offline.

If you cannot deliver a request that way, or this software includes no
addressees, spend one hour online researching an address, recording all your
searches and enquiries as you go, and try any addresses that you find.

If you cannot find any addresses, or if those addresses also fail, that counts
as failure to offer fair terms by the licensor under Paid Use.

## Fair, Reasonable and Non-Discriminatory Terms

Fair, reasonable and non-discriminatory terms may license the software
perpetually or for a term, and may or may not cover new versions of the
software.

If the licensor advertises licence terms and a pricing structure for generally
available paid licences, the licensor proposes licence terms and a price as
advertised, and a customer not affiliated with the licensor has bought a paid
licence for the software on substantially equivalent terms in the past year, the
proposal is fair, reasonable and non-discriminatory.

## Machine-Written Software

Substantial portions of this software were produced by machine at the direction
of the licensor. The licensor says so plainly rather than leaving you to
discover it.

Where a portion of this software has no human author, the licensor claims no
copyright in it. To that extent there is nothing here to license and these terms
do not restrict it, because they cannot. Where these terms do not bind you by
copyright, they bind you by your agreement to them under Acceptance.

If you pass this software on, or pass on anything built from it, you must not
misrepresent machine-written portions as the work of a human author, and you
must not attach a copyright notice to a portion that has no human author.

A machine learning model trained on this software is a derivative of it. See
Training and Models.

## Training and Models

Training a machine learning model on this software is use of this software.

You may train a model on this software. If you do, the model is a derivative of
this software and you must license the model under these terms, and make it
available under them.

Training a model as, or for, an organisation is use for the benefit of that
organisation, and that organisation must qualify under Individual Use, Small
Organisation or Paid Use, exactly as for any other use.

Where you have trained a model on this software, every use of that model by an
organisation that does not qualify under Small Organisation is Paid Use of this
software, and requires a paid licence under these terms.

## Copyright Licence

The licensor grants you a copyright licence to do everything with the software
that would otherwise infringe the licensor's copyright in it, for any purpose
allowed by these terms.

## Notices

You must ensure that anyone who gets a copy of any part of the software from you
also gets a copy of these terms or the URL for them above, as well as copies of
any plain-text lines beginning with `Required Notice:` that the licensor
provided with the software. For example:

> Required Notice: Copyright Yoyodyne Ltd (https://example.com)

## Patent Licence

The licensor grants you a patent licence for the software that covers patent
claims the licensor can license, or becomes able to license, that you would
infringe by using the software.

## Fair Use

You may have "fair use" or "fair dealing" rights for the software under the law.
These terms do not limit them.

## No Other Rights

These terms do not allow you to sublicense or transfer any of your licences to
anyone else, or prevent the licensor from granting licences to anyone else.
These terms do not imply any other licences.

## Patent Defence

If you make any written claim that the software infringes or contributes to
infringement of any patent, your patent licence for the software granted under
these terms ends immediately. If your organisation makes such a claim, your
patent licence ends immediately for work on behalf of your organisation.

## Violations

The first time you are notified in writing that you have violated any of these
terms, or done anything with the software not covered by your licences, your
licences can nonetheless continue if you come into full compliance with these
terms, and take practical steps to correct past violations, within 32 days of
receiving notice. Otherwise, all your licences end immediately.

## No Liability

***As far as the law allows, the software comes as is, without any warranty or
condition, and the licensor will not be liable to you for any damages arising
out of these terms or the use or nature of the software, under any kind of legal
claim.***

## Definitions

The **licensor** is the individual or organisation offering these terms, and the
**software** is the software the licensor makes available under these terms.

**You** refers to the individual or organisation agreeing to these terms.

**Your organisation** is any legal entity, sole proprietorship, or other kind of
organisation that you work for, plus all organisations that have control over,
are under the control of, or are under common control with that organisation.
**Control** means ownership of substantially all the assets of an entity, or the
power to direct its management and policies by vote, contract, or otherwise.
Control can be direct or indirect.

An organisation is an **organisation** whether or not it is incorporated, and
whether or not it exists to make a profit.

**Your licences** are all the licences granted to you for the software under
these terms.

**Use** means anything you do with the software requiring one of your licences.

A **machine learning model** is a program or device that uses data to influence
its future operation, whether or not that data is recognisable in it. Other
names for one are an artificial intelligence, a large language model, and a
model. To **train** one is to supply data to it for the purpose of producing or
improving it.

**Natural person** means a human being, as distinct from an organisation, which
the law may treat as a person but which is not one.

## Meta Licence

Each contributor grants everyone permission to do everything with The Individual
Use Licence that would otherwise infringe their copyright in it, under these
rules:

***As far as the law allows, The Individual Use Licence comes as is, without any
warranty at all. No one involved in writing, reviewing or improving The
Individual Use Licence will be liable to you for any damages related to this
licence grant or use of The Individual Use Licence, for any kind of legal
claim.***

If you make changes to The Individual Use Licence, remove all mention of
"Individual" from your changed version.
